  "label": "Anti-Latino Stereotype",
  "description": "Anti-Latino stereotypes often include associations with criminality, drug trafficking, or chaotic behavior. While the meme does not explicitly state these stereotypes, the context of a '4 car pile-up in Mexico' combined with a mocking reaction may implicitly reinforce negative perceptions of Mexican drivers or the country as a place of disorder. This stereotype is part of the broader cultural context that the meme relies on to be understood and to convey its harmful message.",
